WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.030
An AI agent can answer the texts and calls that customers send to

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:09.798
your numbers, around the clock, and hand the customer to a person when needed.

00:00:09.798 --> 00:00:12.352
It can also reach out to a list itself.

00:00:12.352 --> 00:00:15.020
This use case shows how it fits together.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:19.050
It is a recap, and it points to the videos that show each screen.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.787
This is for managers and AI content managers who want an AI agent

00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:29.186
on the front line.

00:00:29.186 --> 00:00:33.264
It answers every text or call to a number you choose, greets the

00:00:33.264 --> 00:00:35.770
customer, and holds the conversation.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:42.180
Or the AI starts the conversations itself, texting or calling the contacts you load.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:47.393
At the end, the AI picks an outcome from your dispositions and saves

00:00:47.393 --> 00:00:52.700
a summary, and your subject flow runs, just as if an agent had completed the work.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:57.992
When the customer asks for a person, looks like a qualified lead, or

00:00:57.992 --> 00:01:01.982
is frustrated, the AI can hand them to an agent in a queue.

00:01:01.982 --> 00:01:04.990
You can read every conversation afterwards.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:13.062
You need an AI provider connection and a chat deployment.

00:01:13.062 --> 00:01:16.750
Your administrator or AI content manager sets that up.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:23.557
For texts, you need an SMS provider and the features SMS Omnichannel Automation

00:01:23.557 --> 00:01:25.838
and SMS Messaging Channel.

00:01:25.838 --> 00:01:31.610
For calls, you need Telnyx as the phone provider and Telnyx AI Voice Agent.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.790
To answer your numbers, you need Contact Center Inbound Entry Points.

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:41.397
For hand-off to a person, you need Work Distribution for the queues, and

00:01:41.397 --> 00:01:43.760
the messaging workspace for texts.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:53.520
First, create the AI profile under Artificial Intelligence, Profiles, and pick a starting

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.027
point, such as Customer care by text or Answer calls at the front desk.

00:01:58.027 --> 00:02:03.060
Name your business, and fill in the about the business part of the instructions.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:10.410
Second, and optionally, attach documents or data sources, so that it answers from your own knowledge.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:18.140
Third, the number must be on Omnichannel Addresses, with Voice calls or Text messages ticked.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:25.669
Fourth, give the number an inbound, automated subject, with dispositions and a subject flow.

00:02:25.669 --> 00:02:29.958
To allow hand-off, turn on Allow the AI to hand off to a

00:02:29.958 --> 00:02:34.800
live agent, pick the handoff queue, and choose when to escalate.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.997
Make sure agents work the handoff queue.

00:02:41.997 --> 00:02:47.470
Calls ring an agent in the queue, and texts appear in the messaging workspace.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:53.319
Under Inbound entry points, edit the number's entry point, set Route to to

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:58.100
AI agent for texts or AI voice agent for calls, and pick the profile.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:03.390
Pick a business hours calendar if the AI should answer only at certain times.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.769
Or create an automatic activity load with the profile, the channel and the

00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:12.010
number, and add a cadence to follow up on silence.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:18.183
Open a contact's activities and click Review AI conversation to read the transcript.

00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:22.702
The AI handoff and containment report shows how often the AI handed a

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.570
conversation to a person.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:33.589
Call or text the number from your own phone while the entry point is open.

00:03:33.589 --> 00:03:37.865
The AI greets you, or replies to your text after its usual pause.

00:03:37.865 --> 00:03:41.660
Ask a question about your business, and check the answer.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.339
Ask to speak to a person.

00:03:44.339 --> 00:03:49.816
If hand-off is allowed, a text conversation appears in the messaging workspace, or

00:03:49.816 --> 00:03:52.990
the call rings an agent in the handoff queue.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:04:00.080
End the conversation, then open your contact's activities and read it with Review AI conversation.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:08.000
An entry point that is closed does not use the AI.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:14.310
Calls go to voicemail, or are refused, and texts go to people with the closed auto-reply.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.709
A text goes to people instead of the AI when a person already

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:22.849
has an open conversation with the customer on that number, or when the

00:04:22.849 --> 00:04:26.770
customer's last AI conversation there ended less than an hour ago.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.322
Start with a test number and a few colleagues before you point your

00:04:31.322 --> 00:04:32.780
main number at the AI.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:39.545
A profile, a number, outcomes and a hand-off queue, and the AI is

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.155
on the front line.

00:04:41.155 --> 00:04:46.255
Watch the videos on automated SMS and the AI hand-off for each screen.

00:04:46.255 --> 00:04:48.000
Thanks for watching.

